-- title:
--   Cut words inside M at a compact open level U
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, $D$ a set of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, and $\xi$ a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top$ of $(\mathbb{A}_F)^{\times}$ to $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$. Let $U$ be a compact subgroup and $O$ an open subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ with $U = O \cap \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)_{\mathrm{f}}$, where the latter is the kernel of the archimedean projection, and let `tys` assign to each infinite place $w$ of $F$ a finite list of archimedean types. Write `pins` for the data assembled by `productionPinsOf` from $D$, the levels $N \mapsto \mathrm{levelOne}(N) \cap \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)_{\mathrm{f}}$, the Hecke generators `heckeGen` at the finite places and the box `adelicBox` (Borel structures and Haar measures on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ and on $\mathbb{A}_F$, central subgroup $\top$, and the additive Haar measure conditioned on the box). Let $V$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ which is a cuspidal subrepresentation for `pins` and $\xi$, i.e. $V$ lies in the $K$-finite cusp submodule attached to `pins` and $\xi$ and is stable under right translation by finite adelic elements, under right translation by the row-isometry inclusions $\mathrm{rowIsometryInclAt₀}$ at each infinite place, and under right convolution with factorizable test functions that are archimedean bi-finite for some type family. Let $M$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of functions which is (i) stable under right translation by row isometries at every infinite place; (ii) stable under Hecke double-coset sums at level $U$ on its right-$U$-invariant vectors: for $g$ in the finite part and any finite family $\mathrm{reps} : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ whose members lie in $UgU$, whose right $U$-cosets cover $UgU$, and which are pairwise inequivalent modulo $U$ on the right, the function $x \mapsto \sum_i \varphi(x\,\mathrm{reps}\,i)$ lies in $M$ whenever $\varphi \in M$ satisfies $\varphi(xu) = \varphi(x)$ for all $u \in U$; and (iii) stable under right convolution by factorizable test functions $f$ that are archimedean bi-finite of type `tys` and $U$-bi-invariant. Then the infimum of all submodules $W$ that are cuspidal subrepresentations for `pins` and $\xi$ and contain $V \cap L_U \cap A_{\mathrm{tys}} \cap M$, intersected with $L_U \cap A_{\mathrm{tys}}$, is contained in $M$; here $L_U$ denotes the invariants of the right regular representation restricted to $U$ and $A_{\mathrm{tys}} = \bigcap_w \sum_i \mathrm{archTypeSubmoduleAt}(w, \mathrm{tys}.\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i)$ is the archimedean cut submodule.
--
--   This is the "cut words" step at a general compact open level: it says that the cuspidal subrepresentation generated by the $U$-invariant, archimedean-cut part of $V$ lying in $M$ cannot acquire new $U$-invariant vectors of type `tys` outside $M$. It is used in the irreducibility dichotomy for closed cuspidal subrepresentations, [`AutomorphicForm.CuspidalSpectrum.map_inf_eq_bot_or_le_of_isIrreducibleCuspSubrep_of_isClosed`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.CuspidalSpectrum.map_inf_eq_bot_or_le_of_isIrreducibleCuspSubrep_of_isClosed).
